IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`
IMPORT `poa-core`
IMPORT `poa-seat`
IMPORT `poa-seat-attorney`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 1998 (Qld) -- cases from the seat of the attorney answering a claim, with mirror cases: the same
-- facts asked from the claimant's seat (poa-seat.l4) and the attorney's, with answers that agree.
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
--
-- The story continues poa-cases-claimant.l4: Daniel, attorney for financial matters under his mother Margaret's
-- enduring power of attorney of 3 May 2021. HYPOTHETICAL facts throughout.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

`EPA` MEANS `an attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
`general` MEANS `an attorney under a general power of attorney made under this Act`
`AHD` MEANS `an attorney under an advance health directive`
`SHA` MEANS `a statutory health attorney`
`revoked` MEANS `the document has been revoked, wholly or to the extent it gives the power`

§ `s 73 -- conflict transactions (mirror)`

-- Daniel bought Margaret's car with nobody's authorisation (example 1).
#ASSERT `As attorney, was I allowed to enter into this transaction` `the attorney's own interests` `something else` `nobody has authorised it` EQUALS `yes, a conflict transaction entered into without authorisation: the attorney has acted contrary to s 73(1) until it is authorised (s 73(5)); the court may still relieve the attorney (s 105)`
#ASSERT `As attorney, was I allowed to enter into this transaction` `the attorney's own interests` `something else` `nobody has authorised it` EQUALS `Was my attorney allowed to enter into this transaction` `the attorney's own interests` `something else` `nobody has authorised it`
-- The court authorised it afterwards (s 118(3)-(4)).
#ASSERT `As attorney, was I allowed to enter into this transaction` `the attorney's own interests` `something else` `the court authorised it afterwards (s 118(3))` EQUALS `yes, a conflict transaction authorised afterwards: it is taken to be, and always to have been, as valid as if authorised beforehand (s 73(3) or s 118(4))`
#ASSERT `As attorney, was I allowed to enter into this transaction` `the attorney's own interests` `something else` `the court authorised it afterwards (s 118(3))` EQUALS `Was my attorney allowed to enter into this transaction` `the attorney's own interests` `something else` `the court authorised it afterwards (s 118(3))`
-- Daniel and Margaret refinance the house they own as joint tenants (s 73(7)(c)).
#ASSERT `As attorney, was I allowed to enter into this transaction` `the attorney's own interests` `merely that the attorney, in their own right and for the principal, deals with or acquires a joint interest in property, or borrows or guarantees for that` `nobody has authorised it` EQUALS `no: a transaction is not a conflict transaction merely because of that (s 73(7))`

§ `s 86 -- separate property (mirror)`

#ASSERT `Must I keep my property separate from the principal's` `EPA` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the attorney must keep their property separate from the principal's (s 86(1)); not doing so is an offence, up to 300 penalty units`
#ASSERT `Must I keep my property separate from the principal's` `EPA` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Did my attorney have to keep their property separate from mine` `EPA` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I keep my property separate from the principal's` `EPA` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 86(1) does not apply to property the principal and the attorney own jointly (s 86(2)(a))`
#ASSERT `Must I keep my property separate from the principal's` `general` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: Part 3 applies only to enduring powers of attorney (s 83)`

§ `s 97 -- the court's advice`

#ASSERT `Am I protected because I followed the court's advice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: an attorney who acts in compliance with the court's advice, directions or recommendations is taken to have complied with this Act (s 97)`
#ASSERT `Am I protected because I followed the court's advice` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 97 does not protect an attorney who knowingly gave the court false or misleading information relevant to its advice`
#ASSERT `Am I protected because I followed the court's advice` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not settle this under s 97: it protects an attorney acting in compliance with the court's advice, directions or recommendations`

§ `s 98 -- an invalid power (mirror)`

#ASSERT `Am I liable for using a power I did not know was invalid` `EPA` `revoked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an attorney who used the power without knowing it was invalid incurs no liability, to the principal or anyone else, because of the invalidity (s 98(2)); liability for anything else is not affected`
#ASSERT `Am I liable for using a power I did not know was invalid` `EPA` `revoked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Is my attorney liable for acting under an invalid power` `EPA` `revoked` FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I liable for using a power I did not know was invalid` `EPA` `revoked` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 98 gives the attorney no protection on these facts: the attorney knew of the invalidity, knew of an event that invalidated the power, or had reason to believe it was invalid`
#ASSERT `Am I liable for using a power I did not know was invalid` `EPA` `revoked` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Is my attorney liable for acting under an invalid power` `EPA` `revoked` FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I liable for using a power I did not know was invalid` `SHA` `revoked` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not settle this: s 98 does not reach a statutory health attorney (s 98(1))`

§ `s 105 -- relief`

#ASSERT `Can the court relieve me from personal liability` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the court may relieve you from all or part of your personal liability for the breach (s 105(1))`
#ASSERT `Can the court relieve me from personal liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 105 gives no relief on these facts; the court must consider you acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused`
#ASSERT `Can the court relieve me from personal liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 105 gives no relief on these facts; the court must consider you acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused`
#ASSERT `Can the court relieve me from personal liability` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 105 does not arise: you are not, and may not be, personally liable for a breach of this Act`

§ `s 106 -- compensation (mirror)`

#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay compensation or my profits` `EPA` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the court or tribunal may order the attorney to pay compensation for the loss or to account for the profits, but not both for the same exercise of power (s 106(1)-(2)), paid to` `the principal's estate`
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay compensation or my profits` `EPA` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Can I get compensation or the profits from my attorney` `EPA` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay compensation or my profits` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Can I get compensation or the profits from my attorney` `general` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay compensation or my profits` `SHA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 106 does not reach a statutory health attorney (s 106(9))`

§ `Offences (mirror)`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `not keeping the attorney's property separate from the principal's (s 86(1))` EQUALS `the most you can be fined is, in penalty units` 300
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `exercising a power the attorney knows has been revoked (s 71)` EQUALS `the most you can be fined is, in penalty units` 200
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `other conduct` EQUALS `the Act does not settle this: ss 26, 61, 66, 71, 74A and 86 do not make that conduct an offence (other law may)`
-- Mirror: the two seats state the same maximum.
#ASSERT `What offence has my attorney committed` `not keeping the attorney's property separate from the principal's (s 86(1))` EQUALS `an offence; the most the court can impose is, in penalty units` 300

§ `ss 72, 82 -- resigning`

-- Margaret, with capacity: Daniel may resign by signed notice (s 72(1)).
#ASSERT `Can I resign as attorney` `EPA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may resign for the matter by signed notice given to the principal (s 72(1)); another way the law allows also remains (s 72(2))`
-- Margaret with dementia (cannot understand decisions): only with the court's leave (s 82(1)).
#ASSERT `Can I resign as attorney` `EPA` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `only with the court's leave: while the principal has impaired capacity for the matter, an attorney under an enduring document may resign only with the court's leave (s 82(1)); the court may appoint a replacement (s 82(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I resign as attorney` `EPA` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court has given leave, so you may resign for the matter (s 82(1)); the court may appoint a replacement (s 82(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I resign as attorney` `AHD` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `only with the court's leave: while the principal has impaired capacity for the matter, an attorney under an enduring document may resign only with the court's leave (s 82(1)); the court may appoint a replacement (s 82(2))`
-- A general power of attorney: s 82 is for enduring documents only, so s 72 applies even with impaired capacity
-- (a general power is revoked by the principal's impaired capacity anyway, s 18; out of scope).
#ASSERT `Can I resign as attorney` `general` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: you may resign for the matter by signed notice given to the principal (s 72(1)); another way the law allows also remains (s 72(2))`
#ASSERT `Can I resign as attorney` `SHA` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not settle this: ss 72 and 82 do not reach a statutory health attorney`
